python-developer-skills\/#faq-question-1784620380933\",\"position\":2,\"url\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/python-developer-skills\/#faq-question-1784620380933\",\"name\":\"2. How long does it take to become a job-ready Python developer?\",\"answerCount\":1,\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"With consistent practice, most people reach a job-ready level in around 6 to 12 months. The timeline depends on your background, daily effort, and how quickly you build real projects.\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/python-developer-skills\/#faq-question-1784620393928\",\"position\":3,\"url\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/python-developer-skills\/#faq-question-1784620393928\",\"name\":\"3. Which\u00a0skills for\u00a0python\u00a0developer\u00a0are most in demand for freshers?\",\"answerCount\":1,\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Freshers should focus on core Python, OOP, basic data structures, one framework (Django or Flask), Git, and simple frontend basics. Adding\u00a0a data\u00a0science or ML library gives you an extra edge in interviews.\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/python-developer-skills\/#faq-question-1784620409257\",\"position\":4,\"url\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/python-developer-skills\/#faq-question-1784620409257\",\"name\":\"4. Do Python developers need to\u00a0know\u00a0frontend\u00a0technologies?\",\"answerCount\":1,\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Yes, at least the basics. A working knowledge of <a href=\\\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/resources\/html\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noreferrer noopener\\\">HTML<\/a>, CSS, and JavaScript helps Python developers align the server and client sides and is essential for full-stack roles.\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},{\"@type\":\